---
title: "Pick Your Time - The Zero Fog"
permalink: /workshop/schedule/
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{# The schedule step. Reached straight after the opt-in form, which carries the address here in
   sessionStorage rather than in the URL. Copy rule, CEO 2026-08-11: this is a workshop and an
   occurrence of it is a session - the words "webinar" and "training" appear nowhere. #}

{% block head_extras %}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_css %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/pages/replay-3.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/pages/workshop-schedule.css">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<a href="/" class="brand">The Zero Fog</a>
<button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" onclick="toggleTheme()">Light</button>

<div class="replay schedule">

  <p class="eyebrow">Free Workshop</p>

  <h1>Pick the time that suits you</h1>
  {# "About an hour" is the measured length, not a guess: the master runs 3510.73 s - 58:31 -
     read off the file with ffprobe on 2026-08-13. It said 90 minutes until then, which was half
     an hour of somebody's evening claimed under false pretences. Duration figures in this project
     have lied before; if the recording is ever replaced, measure it again before touching this. #}
  <p class="subtitle">It runs about an hour. Times below are in your own timezone.</p>

  <div id="slotStatus" class="slot-status">Loading times…</div>

  <ul id="slotList" class="slot-list" hidden></ul>

  <form id="scheduleForm" class="schedule-form" hidden>
    {# `required` is NOT in this markup, and must never be put back. The row is hidden whenever the
       address already arrived from the landing page, which is the ordinary path through the
       funnel - and a required, empty, display:none field makes the whole form invalid. The
       browser then refuses to submit and cannot show its message either, because it has nothing
       focusable to attach it to, so the button does precisely nothing. That is what a visitor
       coming from the opt-in met on every attempt. The script sets `.required` on this input at
       runtime, and only in the branch where the row is actually shown. #}
    <div id="emailRow" class="field" hidden>
      <label for="scheduleEmail">Where should we send your link?</label>
      <input type="email" id="scheduleEmail" name="email" autocomplete="email"
             placeholder="you@example.com">
    </div>

    {# Honeypot. Bots fill it, people never see it. #}
    <input type="text" name="website" id="scheduleWebsite" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"
           aria-hidden="true">

    <label class="consent">
      <input type="checkbox" id="scheduleConsent" required>
      <span id="consentText">I agree to receive emails about this workshop and can unsubscribe at any time.</span>
    </label>

    <p class="form-error" id="scheduleError" role="alert"></p>

    {# Full width to match the slots and the address field above it - it was the one control in
       the column that hugged its own text and sat against the left edge. #}
    <button type="submit" class="cta-btn cta-btn--full" id="scheduleBtn">Save My Seat</button>
  </form>

  <p class="disclaimer">This is an educational program, not medical treatment. Results vary.</p>

</div>

{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
<script src="/assets/js/pages/workshop-schedule.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
